</WBK>
<BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/></TAB></TXT><BRK/>
<TXT>Conform to applicable AISC specifications for all welds and welding operations.  Provide 316 stainless steel 
anchor bolts and fasteners for all underwater locations.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
</SPT>]<SPT><TTL><SUB>SLUDGE COLLECTORS FOR RECTANGULAR TANKS</SUB></TTL><BRK/>
<NTE><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/>
<NPR>NOTE:  Designer needs to understand the different types of thickener mechanisms 
and make a selection based on manufacturer's recommendation.</NPR><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/></NTE>
<BRK/>
[<SPT><TTL>Rectangular Thickener Mechanism</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<SPT><TTL>General</TTL><BRK/>
<OLG><BRK/>
<OLI>Design the thickener mechanism for continuous duty and exposure to wastewater, scum and sludges containing 
organic and inorganic solids, including vegetable parts, grits, grit, paper and rubber products, rags 
petroleum products, animal fats and greases, industrial solvent, ammonia, and detergents.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI>Provide complete thickener mechanism of sufficient strength and sufficient mechanical ability to operate 
continuously thickening of the [WAS] [sludge] listed in table below at paragraph RECTANGULAR THICKENER 
DESIGN CRITERIA.  Remove the thickened sludge by the flights in a straight path cross collector located 
at the influent end of the tanks.  Convey the thickened solids by the cross collector to a sump located 
at one end of the cross collector trough.  Configure the equipment to allow operation for up to 8 hours 
when the thickener basins are dry.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI>Design both the chain and flight mechanism and the cross collector mechanisms with sufficient strength 
to withstand torque levels occurring at cut-out of the overload device without exceeding allowable stresses, 
causing damage or undue deflection.</OLI><BRK/></OLG>
<BRK/></SPT>
</SPT>]<SPT><TTL>Rectangular Thickener Design Criteria</TTL><BRK/>
<TXT><TAB HEADERROWS="0">
<WBK>
   <STS/>
   <TDA COLUMNCOUNT="2" ROWCOUNT="15">
      <COL AUTOWIDTH="0" WIDTH="257.25"/>
      <COL AUTOWIDTH="0" WIDTH="256.50"/>
